    "message": "Guidelines require all PLHIV to be screened for hypertension risk factors including tobacco, overweight, dyslipidemia, and physical inactivity at every visit. BP is elevated at 146/94 and trace proteinuria is noted. No documentation of cardiovascular risk factor screening, lipid profile, or BMI assessment is recorded. The plan addresses adherence but omits structured hypertension risk assessment and escalation of antihypertensive therapy despite suboptimal control.",
    "issue_type": "guideline_deviation",
    "severity": "moderate",
    "recommended_action": "Screen for hypertension risk factors per guideline. Consider antihypertensive dose increase or addition. Check lipids and assess cardiovascular risk.",
